." Manpage for smi-agent
.TH smi-agent 1 "September 2026" "setmy.info" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
smi-agent \- run an AI agent CLI non-interactively, with defaults for everything
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-agent
.RB [ \-\-agent
.IR AGENT ]
.RB [ \-\-model
.IR MODEL ]
.RB [ \-\-reasoning
.IR LEVEL ]
.RB [ \-\-prompt\-file
.IR FILE ]
.RI [ AGENT_ARG ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B smi-agent
command builds the agent specific model and reasoning options with the same logic as
.BR smi-agent-cli-options (1)
and runs the agent with the same logic as
.BR smi-agent-cli (1).
Every option has a default, so calling it without parameters runs the cheapest configuration:
agent
.BR claude ,
prompt file
.IR TASKLIST.sexp ,
the first model of the agent's model list, reasoning
.BR low .
.PP
Anything that is not one of the options below is passed to the agent CLI unchanged.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-agent \ AGENT
Agent to run:
.BR claude ,
.BR cursor ,
.BR gemini ,
.BR codex ,
.BR codewhale ,
.BR opencode .
Default
.BR claude .
.TP
.BI \-\-model \ MODEL
Model name, validated against the agent's model list in
.IR ai-agents.sh .
Default is the first, least expensive, entry of that list.
.TP
.BI \-\-reasoning \ LEVEL
.BR low ,
.B medium
or
.BR high .
Default
.BR low .
Ignored by agents without a reasoning option.
.TP
.BI \-\-prompt\-file \ FILE
Prompt file in s-expression (Lisp) syntax.
Default
.IR TASKLIST.sexp .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 1
Unknown agent, unknown model, unknown reasoning level, or prompt file not found.
.PP
Otherwise the exit status of the agent CLI.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.B smi-agent
.br
.B smi-agent --model sonnet --reasoning high
.br
.B smi-agent --agent codex --prompt-file PLAN.sexp
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-agent-cli (1),
.BR smi-agent-cli-options (1),
.BR ai (1),
.BR smi-build-tasklist (1)
